        "step_number": 1,
        "text": "Step 1: Simplify the equation by recognizing that \\(2x - 10 = 2(x - 5)\\). Thus, the equation becomes \\((x - 3)^3 + (x - 7)^3 = [2(x - 5)]^3\\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 279,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 281,
        "char_start": 144,
        "effective_step": 2,
        "end_token_index": 122,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 123,
        "step_number": 2,
        "text": "Step 2: Expand the right side of the equation: \\([2(x - 5)]^3 = 8(x - 5)^3\\). The equation now is \\((x - 3)^3 + (x - 7)^3 = 8(x - 5)^3\\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 375,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 377,
        "char_start": 283,
        "effective_step": 3,
        "end_token_index": 165,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 166,
        "step_number": 3,
        "text": "Step 3: Let \\(y = x - 5\\). Then the equation transforms into \\((y + 2)^3 + (y - 2)^3 = 8y^3\\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 510,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 511,
        "char_start": 379,
        "effective_step": 4,
        "end_token_index": 249,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 250,
        "step_number": 4,
        "text": "Step 4: Expand both \\((y + 2)^3\\) and \\((y - 2)^3\\):\n\\[\n(y + 2)^3 = y^3 + 6y^2 + 12y + 8,\n\\]\n\\[\n(y - 2)^3 = y^3 - 6y^2 + 12y - 8.\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 647,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 648,
        "char_start": 513,
        "effective_step": 5,
        "end_token_index": 329,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 330,
        "step_number": 5,
        "text": "Step 5: Add these two expressions together:\n\\[\n(y + 2)^3 + (y - 2)^3 = (y^3 + 6y^2 + 12y + 8) + (y^3 - 6y^2 + 12y - 8) = 2y^3 + 24y.\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 721,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 722,
        "char_start": 650,
        "effective_step": 6,
        "end_token_index": 360,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 361,
        "step_number": 6,
        "text": "Step 6: Substitute this back into the equation:\n\\[\n2y^3 + 24y = 8y^3.\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 867,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 868,
        "char_start": 724,
        "effective_step": 7,
        "end_token_index": 431,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 432,
        "step_number": 7,
        "text": "Step 7: Rearrange the equation to isolate terms involving \\(y\\):\n\\[\n2y^3 + 24y - 8y^3 = 0 \\implies -6y^3 + 24y = 0 \\implies -6y(y^2 - 4) = 0.\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 938,
