  "raw_text": "Step 1: Simplify the equation by recognizing that \\(2x - 10 = 2(x - 5)\\). Thus, the equation becomes \\((x - 3)^3 + (x - 7)^3 = [2(x - 5)]^3\\).\n\nStep 2: Expand the right side of the equation: \\([2(x - 5)]^3 = 8(x - 5)^3\\). The equation now is \\((x - 3)^3 + (x - 7)^3 = 8(x - 5)^3\\).\n\nStep 3: Let \\(y = x - 5\\). Then the equation transforms into \\((y + 2)^3 + (y - 2)^3 = 8y^3\\).\n\nStep 4: Expand both \\((y + 2)^3\\) and \\((y - 2)^3\\):\n\\[\n(y + 2)^3 = y^3 + 6y^2 + 12y + 8,\n\\]\n\\[\n(y - 2)^3 = y^3 - 6y^2 + 12y - 8.\n\\]\n\nStep 5: Add these two expressions together:\n\\[\n(y + 2)^3 + (y - 2)^3 = (y^3 + 6y^2 + 12y + 8) + (y^3 - 6y^2 + 12y - 8) = 2y^3 + 24y.\n\\]\n\nStep 6: Substitute this back into the equation:\n\\[\n2y^3 + 24y = 8y^3.\n\\]\n\nStep 7: Rearrange the equation to isolate terms involving \\(y\\):\n\\[\n2y^3 + 24y - 8y^3 = 0 \\implies -6y^3 + 24y = 0 \\implies -6y(y^2 - 4) = 0.\n\\]\n\nStep 8: Factor the quadratic expression:\n\\[\n-6y(y - 2)(y + 2) = 0.\n\\]\n\nStep 9: Set each factor equal to zero:\n\\[\ny = 0, \\quad y = 2, \\quad y = -2.\n\\]\n\nStep 10: Convert back to \\(x\\) using \\(y = x - 5\\):\n\\[\nx - 5 = 0 \\implies x = 5,\n\\]\n\\[\nx - 5 = 2 \\implies x = 7,\n\\]\n\\[\nx - 5 = -2 \\implies x = 3.\n\\]\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{3, 5, 7}<|im_end|>",
